\pard\sa120\sb120\fs32\b testConnectAndList\b0{\*\bkmkstart testconnectandlist}{\*\bkmkend testconnectandlist}\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Description\b0{\*\bkmkstart description}{\*\bkmkend description}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 Exercises the read-only / connection-lifecycle commands against an appliance, proving they fail gracefully without a session and succeed with one: Test-ServerConnectivity, Connect-OneView, Disconnect-OneView, Get-OneViewConnectionStatus, Get-OneViewServerList, Get-OneViewServerTarget, Get-OneViewVersion, Test-ServerList \i  Running the commands WITHOUT an active OneView session -> they must fail GRACEFULLY with a clear, correct message (never a raw crash). \i0 Connecting (real or -DryRun), then running the SAME commands WITH a session -> they must report success / reachable / data. \i  Disconnecting, then running again -> graceful failure returns. \i0 A matrix of parameter combinations (-OneViewHost, -Filter, -IncludeServerCount, -IdentifierType serial, -DryRun, etc.). The host is taken from -OneViewHost (or prompted). No server names are hard-coded. By default the script runs in SAFE mode: connections are validated with -DryRun and live list commands use -DryRun, so nothing is contacted unless you pass -Live with real credentials. Full logging is written via the module's common logging commands (Initialize-Logging / Get-Logger) under generated/logs/commands/testConnectAndList/.\par
